---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /contact/
title: "Contact"
heading: "Start with an assessment."
description: "Contact Geosustara Enviro Services LLP — Pappanamcode, Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala 695018. Call +91 62824 62332, message on WhatsApp or email geosustara@gmail.com."
lede: "Tell us about your site, your obligations or your research question. We will tell you exactly what is required — and what it takes."
breadcrumbs:
  - text: Home
    url: /
  - text: Contact
faqs:
  - q: "How quickly do you respond to an enquiry?"
    a: "Enquiries sent through this page reach us by email and are normally answered within one working day. If it is urgent, call or send a WhatsApp message on either of the numbers listed — that is always the fastest route."
  - q: "What should I include in a first enquiry?"
    a: "The location of the site, what it is used for, and the obligation or problem you are facing — a notice received, an approval needed, a system that is failing, a study that needs data. Drawings, previous reports and test results are useful but not needed to start."
  - q: "Do you visit the site before quoting?"
    a: "For most work, yes. Environmental scope is very difficult to judge accurately from a description alone, and a short visit usually avoids both over-specifying the study and discovering extra work mid-way."
---
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import svcIcon, arrow -%}

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ct">
      <div class="rv">
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">Office</div>
          <div class="ctv">
            <address style="font-style:normal;line-height:1.7">
              {{ site.contact.addressLine }},<br>
              {{ site.contact.locality }},<br>
              {{ site.contact.region }} {{ site.contact.postalCode }}, {{ site.contact.country }}
            </address>
          </div>
        </div>
        {%- for p in site.contact.phones %}
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">{% if loop.first %}Telephone{% else %}Alternate{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="ctv"><a href="tel:{{ p.e164 }}">{{ p.display }}</a></div>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">WhatsApp</div>
          <div class="ctv"><a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.contact.whatsapp }}" rel="noopener">{{ site.contact.phoneDisplay }} — message us</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">Email</div>
          <div class="ctv"><a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">Entity</div>
          <div class="ctv">{{ site.name }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ctr">
          <div class="ctk">Area served</div>
          <div class="ctv">{{ site.areaServed }} &middot; site work mainly in {{ site.contact.region }}</div>
        </div>

        {%- set directions = "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=" + (site.contact.addressFull | urlencode) %}

        {#- A drawn-once SVG, not a live map. The previous Leaflet + CARTO setup broke when
            CARTO began requiring an API key and started stamping "API KEY REQUIRED" across
            the tiles. This makes no request at runtime, costs ~13 KB gzipped against
            Leaflet's 144 KB, and cannot expire. Regenerate with
            `python .tooling/build-locator-map.py`. -#}
        <figure class="locator">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/img/locator-map.svg' | url }}" width="920" height="613"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Locator map of Thiruvananthapuram. The Geosustara office is marked at
                    Pappanamcode, about 4 km east-south-east of the city centre, with the
                    Arabian Sea coast to the west.">
          <figcaption>
            <span>{{ site.map.note }} &middot; map data &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors</span>
            <a class="btn btn--out" href="{{ directions }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Open in Google Maps {{ arrow() }}</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p class="form-note map-note">The marker is at neighbourhood level, not the door.
          Please call ahead — the lanes here are easier described than mapped.</p>
      </div>

      {% include "partials/contact-form.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--tint">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:900px">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="label">Before you write</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Getting a useful answer<br>on the first reply.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq rv">
      {%- for f in faqs %}
      <details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ f.q }}</summary>
        <div class="a">{{ f.a }}</div>
      </details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- No service card grid here: the form's own dropdown already lists all six, and repeating
    the summaries would put them on a fourth URL. -#}
